WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:03.840
An ion is just an atom,
or a small group of atoms,

2
00:00:03.890 --> 00:00:06.120
carrying an electric charge.

3
00:00:06.170 --> 00:00:10.560
Ions dissolve in water, so they are
found all through living things:

4
00:00:10.610 --> 00:00:14.310
in cytoplasm, in blood, in a plant's sap.

5
00:00:14.360 --> 00:00:19.940
Next to a protein or a strand of
DNA, each one is tiny and simple.

6
00:00:19.990 --> 00:00:24.390
So why can running short of one
simple charged particle stop a cell,

7
00:00:24.440 --> 00:00:27.230
or a whole plant, from working properly?

8
00:00:27.280 --> 00:00:30.110
In this mission, you'll
follow ions to work,

9
00:00:30.160 --> 00:00:32.700
building DNA and ATP.

10
00:00:32.750 --> 00:00:36.700
Then you'll see what happens
when one ion runs short.

11
00:00:36.750 --> 00:00:41.390
Your mission: explain why running
short of one ion can stop a cell,

12
00:00:41.440 --> 00:00:43.810
or a whole plant, from working properly.
